# What `docker manifest inspect` prints on stderr when it fails against a registry, exactly as docker
# 29.4.0 printed it on 2026-10-22 (task 5.1 of add-sandbox-base-image), with no registry login:
# `manifest-unknown` from ghcr for a tag missing from an existing public package, `denied` from ghcr
# for a package not yet created, `no-such-manifest-*` docker's text for a registry's not-found
# (recorded from other registries, ghcr's answer to a logged-in client unrecorded), `no-such-host`
# against an unresolvable registry name.
# One section per answer: its lines up to the blank line that separates it from the next one.

[manifest-unknown]
manifest unknown

[no-such-manifest-final]
no such manifest: ghcr.io/oinsio/gnomish-sandbox-base:0.2.0

[no-such-manifest-pre]
no such manifest: ghcr.io/oinsio/gnomish-sandbox-base:0.3.0-rc.1

[denied]
Get "https://ghcr.io/v2/oinsio/gnomish-sandbox-base/manifests/0.2.0": denied

[no-such-host]
failed to configure transport: error pinging v2 registry: Get "https://no-such-registry.invalid/v2/": dial tcp: lookup no-such-registry.invalid: no such host
